{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/883240-idea-beast-against-abyssal-cults","id":883240,"title":"Idea: Beast Against Abyssal Cults","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-05T15:06:06-07:00","id":883240,"title":"Idea: Beast Against Abyssal Cults","content":"<br /> \u201cCome, Come warm yourself to our fire. We were waiting for you.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t make this face, and don\u2019t be so surprised. You knew you were called, there was a restlessness in you, an urge of leaving your hunting grounds and come here in the ass-end of Massachusetts. There were restless dreams, images of horrors even beyond those you committed or commit when you\u2019re hungry. You saw the dances, the revels, the feasts, the prostrations and the venerations. You heard names screamed in languages not of this world and had the feeling terrible things were about to happen. Perhaps you consulted your friends, described the symbols. Perhaps one of the sorcerers told you of the meaning of Nemean Lion, perhaps a wolf shuddered at the thought of the anti-wendigo. Or perhaps you simply followed your instinct to come here where you needed.<br /> <br /> Fear not! We\u2019re on your side. We are kin. Indeed, it is we who sent the message through the Dream. A sort of signal like when wolves howl when they see a juicy prey for the pack, or a threat for their safety. Each of us here is like you. We know what you are. We know the pitiless hunger that gnaws at your bones, we know the sins we must commit to avoid our souls to feed without discrimination, we know the struggle with what we are.<br /> <br /> We don\u2019t know why we were created, why the things inside us were created. We bleat about teaching humanity a lesson and for some of us their needs suit themselves to this goal, but in truth we feed on what diet our souls requires, be it innocent blood or guilty flesh. Sometimes we go too far but gain the freedom to not have to feed for a longer time than usual. Gorge yourself too often though and the universe breeds champions to make your gluttony ends. It\u2019s the way of thing spanning from the beginning and continuing until the world ends.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to the town near us. Howard\u2019s Rock it is called. One of these little hamlets with a dreadful history. Which will end in a few days after we crash the place. Before the week ends, this place will exist no more or we will be all in the ground. In either case we\u2019ll have done our duty.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t understand yet. Let me explain: There are things more awful than us in this vast world we share with bloodsuckers, werewolves, sorcerers and many other things. There are things who make our little predations or even our large ones seem like children\u2019s games. This town is one of them. To be more precise they worship one of them. They are a cult. A cannibal cult who believe their grotesque meals will actually bring a universe where their sickness is the norm.<br /> <br /> Is this so surprising we would object to such a thing? We who called you encountered members of this cult and tracked them here. Some were polite enough to answer all our questions while some of our contacts explained the rest.<br /> <br /> If you want proof, we\u2019re still preparing ourselves. You can read the texts we uncovered, the items we found. You can even go to Boston and ask the sorcerers here about the Scribe of Blasphemy, about the Red Word and the Prince of the 100 000 Leaves. Some will even answer to you truthfully. They don\u2019t know what we discovered here. They believe the cult extinct but have only exterminated the brazen and idiot ones.<br /> <br /> The rest is here, the whole town worship anti-history and seek to replace the timeline with one more to their liking. At least it\u2019s what their cultists bleated when we interrogated them.<br /> <br /> What we will be doing is a monstrous thing, don\u2019t get me wrong. We will slaughter everyone to toothless old men to toothless infants. We\u2019ll burn their libraries, smash their idols and salt the ashes when we\u2019re done. We\u2019ll find a way to cast down the towers of their temple or at least we\u2019ll be its guardians and protectors until the sorcerers can figure something to do.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll teach humanity to stay outside the tainted zone, to not investigate and risk being exposed to the taint. In the worst case they\u2019ll come to kill us, bring back the riches of our Lairs and not push the matter further.<br /> <br /> And if we fail in our attack? Well at least we\u2019ll teach these cultists they still can know fear. That their master can\u2019t protect them and even their greatest temple is not safe from attack.<br /> <br /> You asked before why were we created. I think it\u2019s for cases like that. When wounds are dealt to the world that must be cleansed by sword and fire. When comes the need for monsters to hunt monsters without remorse or pity.<br /> <br /> No rest, no mercy, no matter what.<br /> <br /> <b>Thoughts?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T02:06:12-07:00","id":883599,"title":"","content":"It is an interesting concept to say the least. I am just imaging the horror if cultists brought forth beings of the abyss. The beasts feel no connection - these are not kin (personal opinion) but worse than an unchained these are not just not kin but anti kin. These creatures do not belong, no beast could make mistaken that as they see kin twisted into a form that does not belong.<br /> <br /> Hard for me to describe right but I feel that the &quot;they are worse than not kin&quot; could truly drive home the horror and urgency to eradicate and raze the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T03:55:23-07:00","id":883632,"title":"","content":"I like it. Not least because I can see pretty much the same speech coming from the mouth of a Hero. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T05:36:55-07:00","id":883663,"title":"","content":"Could even be interesting if the Beasts don't view the Red Word cultists as fundamnetally different. I mean, the Abyss is often talked about using a myth structure not a million miles away from the Dark Mother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T08:00:33-07:00","id":883789,"title":"","content":"I don't see the mythic structure of the Abyss, to be frank.<br /> <br /> And the Prince of 100 000 Leaves is something Beasts would loathe because in a way, a world where predation is encouraged would be good for them. It's just the Prince's world is disgusting to anyone who still keep to humanish morality;<br /> <br /> Also what I like with the idea of Beasts going against the Abyss is it's an epic goal I feel is somewhat missing from the game. Teaching humanity lessons is recognized by Beasts as a post facto rationalization which would get them to ask the purpose of their existence.<br /> <br /> Keeping the world safe from worse monsters a la Owerewolves or Alucard could be a good thing for a social splat to be about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T15:14:41-07:00","id":884111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/883240-idea-beast-against-abyssal-cults?p=883789#post883789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the mythic structure of the Abyss, to be frank.<br /> <br /> And the Prince of 100 000 Leaves is something Beasts would loathe because in a way, a world where predation is encouraged would be good for them. It's just the Prince's world is disgusting to anyone who still keep to humanish morality;<br /> <br /> Also what I like with the idea of Beasts going against the Abyss is it's an epic goal I feel is somewhat missing from the game. Teaching humanity lessons is recognized by Beasts as a post facto rationalization which would get them to ask the purpose of their existence.<br /> <br /> Keeping the world safe from worse monsters a la Owerewolves or Alucard could be a good thing for a social splat to be about.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree. I would also like to see how specific Abyssals could mess around with assumptions on part of the Beasts. For example, an Abyssal that infects peoples' minds and completely changes how they feel and act upon fear (and thus how Beasts can Feed) would be very scary. Now I'm trying to imagine how the Abyss would distort a Hero. There is a Merit called Liar that gives you the Open Condition for Abyssals. Its only prerequisite is Integrity, which Heroes have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:43:44-07:00","id":884962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/883240-idea-beast-against-abyssal-cults?p=883789#post883789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the mythic structure of the Abyss, to be frank.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the primordial chaos that is suppressed by the creation of the ordered Supernal; the same way the Dark Mother draws on the images of Tiamat and other similiar type of mythology*.<br /> <br /> I wasn't criticising your idea, just offering an alternative possibility to the one Mr.F.I.X. offered about how Beasts would react to Abyssal cultists. Even then, just because they might register as similiar to you, doesn't mean you're down with what they do. It's one thing for Beasts to do terrible things, it's another to see normal humans eating each other.<br /> <br /> *Chaoskampf was the mythological structure I was thinking of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","user":"Michael","date":".  clarified what I meant 05-08-2016, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:18:45-07:00","id":884982,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> <br /> Ah I see the mythic role of the Abyss yes. I understood mythic structure as &quot;the Annunaki follow mythic rules for their anti-universes&quot;. <br /> <br /> But yes I'm agreeing with you, in fact there could be Beasts totally down with that the Abyss is and cultists themselves.<br /> <br /> But then I'm of the opinion Beasts should be able to choose what sort of creatures they want to be Kin with, to better or for worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}